# CAT1-037 · SDS Chemical Compatibility Advisor

Decision support only. Confirm with a qualified person.

## What you can run today

Phases 0 and 1 provide a local FastAPI home page, a SQLite schema, a PDF import command and three ways to split SDS text while preserving its source. The CLI is the entry point for loading PDFs. The home page displays the project name and disclaimer. Storage verdicts, cited PPE and emergency cards, review screens and JSON downloads belong to later phases.

## Set up and reproduce the demo

Use a Linux CPU machine with Python 3.11. The dependency freeze was produced with Python 3.11.18. Run these commands from the repository root in Bash. Installation needs access to the pinned packages or a pre-populated wheelhouse. After installation, extraction and chunking run locally with the bundled tokenizer.

```sh
python3.11 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python -m pytest -q
python -m app.ingest.load fixtures/
python -m app.ingest.load fixtures/
python -m uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000
```

Visit http://localhost:8000. Both entry points open advisor.db relative to the working directory. On a fresh database, the first import writes seven versions belonging to six products. The second prints seven duplicate messages. To reproduce a fresh import without deleting prior work, use a fresh checkout and run from its root.

